 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Requests in one process share the `sessions` instance in
+[`larder/session_store.py`](../../larder/session_store.py), following the decision to
+[keep sessions in process memory](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-process-memory.md).
+
+## Known limits
+
+- [Sessions disappear across processes and restarts](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-process-memory.md#consequences).
+  Members must log in again and may need to rebuild their pantry order. Sticky routing can reduce logouts between
+  processes; schedule restarts outside opening hours to reduce disruption.
+- The store does not enforce the [session lifetime](#lifetime) or evict old entries. Callers must check and renew
+  expiry; restarting the process frees its session memory and logs members out.
 
